  <h2>The community</h2>
  <p>
    NaN is a closed, paid community of builders sharing dedicated GPUs to run open models. Access is
    limited to the real capacity of the cluster: when it fills up, we open a waitlist. Every member gets a
    personal, non-transferable API key.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not share, resell or transfer your API key.</li>
    <li>Do not abuse the shared cluster or attempt to exceed the published limits.</li>
    <li>NaN is inference, not training: use the cluster to run models, not to fine-tune them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Membership and payments</h2>
  <p>
    Membership is a monthly subscription with taxes included, month to month, with no commitment. You can
    cancel anytime; access runs until the end of the paid period.
  </p>
  <p id="workspace-backups">
    <strong>Workspace backups.</strong> Workspaces have <strong>no backups unless the workspace backup add-on is
    active</strong>. With the add-on, a snapshot of the workspace disk is taken once a day and kept for 7 days.
    Snapshots are crash-consistent: restoring one is equivalent to the machine losing power at the moment the
    snapshot was taken, so data the workspace had not yet written to disk is not included and running databases
    recover as after a power cut. Restoring a snapshot brings back everything that was on the disk at that time,
    including any access you configured yourself (for example SSH keys or SSH server settings you added); only
    your current NaN SSH key is re-applied by the platform. Enabling the add-on charges the first payment right away (prorated to the
    renewal date when it is added to a slot subscription); turning it off removes it immediately with no refund
    for the current month. Turning the add-on off or deleting the workspace deletes all its snapshots
    permanently. If the workspace's slot ends, or a free workspace loses the membership benefit, the add-on stops
    being billed and the existing snapshots are kept until the workspace itself is deleted at the end of its
    grace period; they are then deleted permanently and cannot be recovered.
  </p>

